  "mainText": "PERFORMANCE AND GOALS\n\nTurn activity into management insight.\n\nCORO Performance connects hours, budgets, workload, goals and variances to inform management decisions.\n\nDiscover CORO Performance\n01\nWhere does time go?\n\nHours by mandate, activity and team member make effort visible.\n\n02\nWhere are the variances?\n\nComparing budgets with planned and actual hours reveals gaps.\n\n03\nWhat is our capacity?\n\nWorkload and planning support assignment decisions.\n\n04\nWhich goals are progressing?\n\nGoals and KPIs provide a shared view of progress.\n\nANALYTICAL WINDOW\n\nAnswer management questions\nCORO Performance analytical window\nACTIVITY\nMEASURE\nVARIANCE\nINSIGHT\nDECISION\nPerformance ≠ CORO Index\n\nPERFORMANCE\n\nActivity · Workload · Budgets · Goals\n\nRESILIENCE\n\nPreparedness · Capacity for events\n\nPerformance primarily measures activity, capacity and goals. Resilience progressively addresses organizational preparedness for events. Both may meet in a Network view while remaining distinct concepts.\n\nMeasure to decide. Decide to progress.\n\nTHIS PART OF THE PLATFORM\n\nA connected product foundation\nDocuments\n\nStructures data and deliverables.\n\nExplore\nProjects\n\nOrganizes mandates and work.\n\nExplore\nPerformance\n\nMeasures activity, goals and capacity.\n\nExplore\nClient\n\nMakes information accessible to clients.\n\nExplore\n\nFAQ\n\nFrequently asked questions\nWhat does CORO Performance measure?\n\nActivity, hours, budgets, capacity, goals and operational variances.\n\nIs it a resilience index?\n\nNo. Operational performance and organizational preparedness are distinct concepts."
 },
